# Cursor Rules for ops-wiki-foundation

All rules and context are maintained in a single source of truth: AGENTS.md.
Read and follow every instruction in AGENTS.md before generating or modifying code or documentation.

Key points:
- This is a Markdown-first operational wiki. All docs live in docs/ with YAML frontmatter.
- Never include real PII, credentials, or secrets. Use fictional data in all examples.
- Every doc must pass `python3 scripts/validate_docs.py` before committing.
- Field values must conform to schemas/required-fields.yml (including field_constraints).
- Use templates from templates/ when creating new pages.
- Scripts require Python 3.9+ and use only PyYAML as a dependency.
- When creating a new doc, set last_reviewed to today's date.
- When editing an existing doc, update last_reviewed to today's date.
- Use ATX-style headings, one blank line around blocks, end files with a trailing newline.
